-- title:
--   Distinct restrictions of the two Gauss branches to K₁
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M \ge 5$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137), the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 (M*p))` of $q$-expansion ratios for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$; let $K_1$ be the corresponding field for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, and assume $K_1 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is an $A$-algebra domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi$; $K$ and $K_1$ are $A$-algebras compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ and $j_1 \in K_1$ be non-zero elements whose images in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ are both the coefficientwise image of $j_q = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } jNumQ)$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ admitting a Gauss presentation: there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot \hat{y} = \hat{x}$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, where $\hat{\,\cdot\,}$ denotes the image of a power series over $A$ in Laurent series over $L$. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ such that $\sigma(j)$ has Laurent expansion the image of $j_q$ under the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ (the ring map [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) rescaling exponents by $p$), such that $\sigma$ preserves the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, such that the pullback $\sigma^{*}W_0$ differs from $W_0$, and such that for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ with non-zero reduction both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $\sigma^{*}W_0$. Then the pullbacks of $W_0$ and of $\sigma^{*}W_0$ along the inclusion $K_1 \hookrightarrow K$ are different valuation subrings of $K_1$.
--
--   Read geometrically, this says that the Gauss (multiplicative) branch of the special fibre of $X_1(Mp)$ over the given discrete valuation ring and its image under the level-$p$ involution lie over two different branches of the special fibre of the floor curve attached to $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, the branches being recorded as valuation subrings of the $q$-expansion function fields. It feeds the analysis of the components of the special fibre and of the action of the diamond automorphisms on the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$.
